From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JJ Furman <jfurman@google.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:37:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Define CLANG_BUILD_STATIC on Windows in Clang's Bazel overlay

Upstream clang/include/clang/Support/Compiler.h gates CLANG_ABI on
CLANG_BUILD_STATIC (unlike llvm/Support/Compiler.h, which also checks
LLVM_ENABLE_LLVM_EXPORT_ANNOTATIONS), causing CLANG_ABI to expand to
__declspec(dllimport) on Windows static Bazel builds. Define
CLANG_BUILD_STATIC on @llvm-project//clang:support for Windows so all
Clang libraries and downstream consumers link statically without
invalidating cached @llvm-project//llvm targets.
---
 utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/clang/BUILD.bazel | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/clang/BUILD.bazel b/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/clang/BUILD.bazel
--- a/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/clang/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/clang/BUILD.bazel
@@ -2324,6 +2324,10 @@ cc_library(
     hdrs = glob([
         "include/clang/Support/*.h",
     ]),
+    defines = select({
+        "@platforms//os:windows": ["CLANG_BUILD_STATIC"],
+        "//conditions:default": [],
+    }),
     includes = ["include"],
     deps = [
         "//llvm:Support",
--
